Session 6, 2026-09-05, New Holland tractor's own built-in VT, alone on the
bus. Firmware: isobus-tc-client @ 935de81 (AgIsoStack vendor patch #3 for
the control-function eviction bug + VT log level Warning -> Info).

FIRST CONFIRMATION THAT #17's FIX WORKS. Compare Session 5's captures, where
vtstat froze at 4 within ~2s and Status Timeout fired every single time.
Here the VT connects and holds for the entire capture, with vtstat climbing
steadily at ~1 Hz -- i.e. the terminal's status broadcasts are arriving AND
still being dispatched to our listener, which is exactly what the eviction
bug used to break.

Operator confirmed live on screen: working set rendered, plough working
width adjustments reflected in real time. The "VT: Wider/Narrower pressed"
lines are those adjustments -- first field verification of the soft-key
path (990e23b) too.

Timestamps are seconds since the logging script attached to COM4. The board
was already booted when the script attached, so t=0 is not board reset.

Trimmed to the interesting parts: connect, a stretch of steady-state, the
operator's soft-key presses, and the tail before the InCommand 1200 was
powered on (see run 3 for what happened then).

